1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,395
Mulberry silk is one of four.

2
00:00:02,395 --> 00:00:11,888
The three wild silks come from other moths: tasar on sal and Terminalia, eri on castor, and muga, the golden silk of Assam.

3
00:00:11,888 --> 00:00:20,625
The eri moth walks out of an open cocoon, so eri silk is made without killing the pupa, and it must be spun, not reeled.

4
00:00:20,625 --> 00:00:26,289
Nepal's centre is at Khopasi in Kavre, producing about thirty nine tonnes a year.

